Z||000000||Haze_Performance||08-31-2001||01:19 AM||||The Indy is back on the road!!!! It was a lousy day. I had a local shop install a water pump & alternator. For one thing the fan wont kick on now. I helped them flush the system (correctly) but the fan just wont kick on. It works when I use the A/C. I'm going to change the thermostat switch this weekend. That was lousy part 1. Now since the mechanics love to leave grease on your paint, I drove it right over to Turtle Wax car wash. (About 100 feet from the shop) Well I parked the car & went inside to pay. They pull the car up, prep it & pull it on the track. The STUPID A$$ kid left the car in park!!! It drug the car all the way through the wash!!!!  The good thing is that the wheel thats on the concrete rolled foward (passengers side) the other wheel just spun backwards on the wet roller. After going postal on a stupid 17 year old manager... (who didn't care about anything I said) he wrote up a report saying if there's something wrong in the near future, they will address it at that time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>I will NEVER have another shop work, wash or touch in anyway my car again!!!<P><BR>Thank You.... I just had to vent a little.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">             <BR></A><BR><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||11
Z||000001||MikeSchaefer||08-31-2001||01:26 AM||||Bummer Haze, but I'm glad to hear that you have her up and running again.<BR>Good luck with the fans, mine are still screwy on the 84 after countless hours of tinkering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Mike S||||reg||1
