Z||000006||artherd||08-31-2001||02:56 AM||||I always pull the wheels when I take my car to a tire shop for example. (I leave them the wheels, not the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Buisnesses have insurence for these reasons, if anything happens to your car, be sure to hammer on them, leaving anything in park like that is just criminal negligence.  Way beyond stupid.<P>Good advice, don't give your keys to anyone who dosen't have 'Fiero' in the name!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Monkeyman||08-31-2001||06:43 AM||||Sorry to hear about your troubles, Haze, but I'm glad to hear that your Indy is finally roadworthy.  Since I'm mechanically challenged, I let the local shop do all the work on 4Play.  If anyone ever needs work done to their Fiero around my neck of the woods, I recommend Dorias Chevrolet.  Damn good folks.  Knowledgeable, friendly, etc, etc.  Just tell them that I sent ya.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||08-31-2001||12:33 PM||||I would go get the punk manager's boss's name.  Run it up their chain of command.  Someone will surely car that they could have screwed up your car - not to mention caring about how little the manager did to make things right.  I'd make them pay for you to take the car to the dealer for an "inspection" to make sure nothing is damaged.  Also, make sure the upper management knows you intend to broadcast your experiences with them with as many car clubs and enthusiasts as you can.  Hit them in the pocketbook!||||reg||8
